# ---> local tooling state
# Agent tooling keeps rules, prompts, skills and chat history in a directory
# named after the tool. That is state for whoever is working in the tree, not
# part of it, and `git add -f` is there for a rules file the project decides to
# share. Aider writes its history beside the config file instead of in a
# directory of its own.
.aider*
